;; spec:   §2 (types §2.15, §4.4, §8.1, §8.5)
;; expect: accept
;; result: 107
;; audit:  clean
;; (dyn Q e) for a scalar e. The typing rule admits it: types §2.15
;; "(dyn P e)  e : S with the instance (P S) resolved at generalisation
;; ⇒ (dyn P)", and scalars have instances (§2.12; a user protocol may be
;; implemented for i64 and unit, syntax §3.10). The two values are stored
;; in a vector and dispatched: 7 + 100 = 107.
;;
;; Observed (fibref run):
;;   result: 107
;;   audit:  clean=true leak-cycles=0 leaks=0 errors=0
;; fibref is right (it dispatches on the value's run-time type, §4.5).
;; The finding is the compiled mapping, which cannot run this program
;; (method.md rule 6):
;;   types §8.5: "(dyn P e) builds { e, (load ptr @P.vt.K) } ... Retain
;;   and release of a (dyn P) value act on obj."
;;   types §8.1: "(dyn P) | { ptr ptr } by value: object, vtable".
;; For e : i64 the obj word is the integer 7, so the retain that storing
;; the dyn into the vector's array performs (E2, and conj's array-with)
;; reads a count header at address 7; for e : unit there is no value at
;; all ("unit | no value: void result, no argument"). A heap-enum box, as
;; §8.1 does for (Option i64), or a rule that (dyn P e) needs an object e,
;; is missing. The same holds for (dyn P e) with e a field-less enum (an
;; i32 variant index). Diagnosis: spec (types §8.5 / §2.15).
(defprotocol Q (q (self) -> i64))
(impl Q i64 (q (self) self))
(impl Q unit (q (self) 100))

(defun sum (xs: (Vec (dyn Q)))
  (loop ((i 0) (acc 0))
    (if (< i (count xs)) (recur (+ i 1) (+ acc (q (nth xs i)))) acc)))

(defun main () -> i64 (sum [(dyn Q 7) (dyn Q ())]))
